@lang en
IMPORT `tasco-vn19-ch4-claims`

-- Tests for Chapter I: Articles 1 to 6 and the operative definitions of Article 2. Every expected
-- value was worked by hand from the source before the assertion was run, never copied from an
-- evaluation; the working is in the comment above each group. A failing assertion is a finding,
-- never a value to edit. Both sides of every threshold the chapter prints are tested.

§ `Tests, Chapter I`

§§ `Article 2.30 and 2.3, ages`

-- 2.30 counts by the last birthday BEFORE the day (fork F2): born 1 Jan 1966, on 1 Jan 2026 the 60th
-- birthday is that day and does not count, so 59; on 2 Jan, 60.
#ASSERT `the age under Article 2.30` (YMD 1966 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 59
#ASSERT `the age under Article 2.30` (YMD 1966 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 2) EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the age under Article 2.30` (YMD 1990 3 15) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 35
-- 2.3 "từ đủ 18 tuổi": completed years, the birthday itself counting.
#ASSERT `completed years of age` (YMD 2008 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `completed years of age` (YMD 2008 1 2) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 17

§§ `Article 1.1, from 1 to 65, over 60 only on continuous renewal from 60`

GIVEN `birth date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A claim`
`a claim by a new insured born on` `birth date` MEANS
    `with the insured` (`a healthy Vietnamese insured born on` `birth date`) `the illness stay claim`

GIVEN `birth date` IS A DATE
      `contract` IS A `The contract`
GIVETH A `A claim`
`a claim by a renewing insured born on` `birth date` `under` `contract` MEANS
    `with the contract` `contract`
        (`with the history` (`a renewal of` `the 2025 standard contract` `continuous since` (YMD 2025 1 1))
            (`a claim by a new insured born on` `birth date`))

-- Start date 1 Jan 2026. Lower edge: age 0 is out, age 1 is in.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`a claim by a new insured born on` (YMD 2025 6 1)))
#ASSERT `Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`a claim by a new insured born on` (YMD 2024 12 31))
-- 60 is not "over 60": a new insured aged 60 is in. Born 1 Jan 1965 is 60 on 1 Jan 2026 (F2).
#ASSERT `Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`a claim by a new insured born on` (YMD 1965 6 1))
#ASSERT `Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`a claim by a new insured born on` (YMD 1965 1 1))
-- 61, new: out. 61, renewing continuously since 1 Jan 2025 (aged 60 then): in.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`a claim by a new insured born on` (YMD 1964 6 1)))
#ASSERT `Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`a claim by a renewing insured born on` (YMD 1964 6 1) `under` `the standard contract`)
-- 61, renewing, but the scope C sum insured lowered from 20 to 10 million at renewal: continuity is
-- broken (Article 5(3), fork F27), and the insured is out (finding X5).
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`a claim by a renewing insured born on` (YMD 1964 6 1) `under` (`a 2026 contract insuring` (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 10000000))))
-- Upper edge: 65 renewing (continuously since 1 Jan 2021, aged 60 then) is in; 66 renewing is out.
-- Born 31 Dec 1959 is 66 on 1 Jan 2026. (The first draft of this test used the 2025 start, when this
-- insured was already 64, which contradicted the scenario it described; the facts were corrected,
-- not the expected value. NOTES.md section 6.)
#ASSERT `Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`with the history` (`a renewal of` `the 2025 standard contract` `continuous since` (YMD 2021 1 1)) (`a claim by a new insured born on` (YMD 1960 6 1)))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`a claim by a renewing insured born on` (YMD 1959 12 31) `under` `the standard contract`))
-- 65 renewing, but continuous participation began at 61: out ("from 60").
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`with the history` (`a renewal of` `the 2025 standard contract` `continuous since` (YMD 2021 6 2)) (`a claim by a new insured born on` (YMD 1960 6 1))))

GIVEN n IS A `A nationality and residence`
GIVETH A `The insured person`
`Ms Lan, of nationality` n MEANS
    `The insured person` WITH
        `nationality and residence`                  IS n
        `date of birth`                              IS YMD 1990 3 15
        `suffering from a neurological disease`      IS FALSE
        `suffering from a psychiatric disease`       IS FALSE
        `suffering from leprosy`                     IS FALSE
        `suffering from cancer`                      IS FALSE
        `permanent disability or injury, in percent` IS 0
        `in a period of treatment for illness or injury` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`with the insured` (`Ms Lan, of nationality` `neither`) `the illness stay claim`))
#ASSERT `Article 1.1, the insured meets the conditions for joining` (`with the insured` (`Ms Lan, of nationality` `a foreigner residing lawfully in Vietnam`) `the illness stay claim`)

§§ `Article 1.2, persons Tasco does not accept`

GIVEN `cancer`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `percent`   IS A NUMBER
      `treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The insured person`
`Ms Lan, with` `cancer` `percent` `treatment` MEANS
    `The insured person` WITH
        `nationality and residence`                  IS `Vietnamese`
        `date of birth`                              IS YMD 1990 3 15
        `suffering from a neurological disease`      IS FALSE
        `suffering from a psychiatric disease`       IS FALSE
        `suffering from leprosy`                     IS FALSE
        `suffering from cancer`                      IS `cancer`
        `permanent disability or injury, in percent` IS `percent`
        `in a period of treatment for illness or injury` IS `treatment`

#ASSERT `Article 1.2, a person Tasco does not accept` (`Ms Lan, with` TRUE 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT `Article 1.2, a person Tasco does not accept` (`Ms Lan, with` FALSE 50 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1.2, a person Tasco does not accept` (`Ms Lan, with` FALSE 49 FALSE))
#ASSERT `Article 1.2, a person Tasco does not accept` (`Ms Lan, with` FALSE 0 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1.2, a person Tasco does not accept` `Ms Lan`)
#ASSERT `Article 1, the insured may be insured` `the illness stay claim`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1, the insured may be insured` (`with the insured` (`Ms Lan, with` FALSE 0 TRUE) `the illness stay claim`))

§§ `Article 2.3, the policyholder`

#ASSERT `Article 2.3, the policyholder qualifies` `an individual policyholder`
#ASSERT `Article 2.3, the policyholder qualifies` `an employer`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2.3, the policyholder qualifies` (`a policyholder` (JUST (YMD 2008 1 2)) FALSE))
#ASSERT `Article 2.3, the policyholder qualifies` (`a policyholder` (JUST (YMD 2008 1 1)) FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 2.3, the policyholder qualifies` (`a policyholder` NOTHING FALSE)

§§ `Article 2.8, 2.12, 2.16, 2.17, 2.19, definitions`

#ASSERT `the sum insured for` `scope C` `under` `the special contract` EQUALS JUST 50000000
#ASSERT `the sum insured for` `scope A` `under` (`a 2026 contract insuring` NOTHING (JUST 1) (JUST 1)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Article 2.12, a pre-existing condition` `a pre-existing condition`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2.12, a pre-existing condition` `an ordinary illness`)
#ASSERT `Article 2.12, a pre-existing condition` (`The illness` WITH `a special disease` IS FALSE, `treated within the 3 years before the start date` IS FALSE, `symptoms or onset before the start date, known to the insured` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `Article 2.16, a doctor` `a licensed doctor`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2.16, a doctor` (`The treating doctor` WITH `holds a lawful practising licence recognised by Vietnamese law` IS TRUE, `treating within the licence and the field of training` IS TRUE, `relation to the insured` IS `a spouse, parent, parent-in-law or child of the insured`, `registered to practise as required` IS TRUE))
#ASSERT `Article 2.17, a medical facility` `a general hospital`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2.17, a medical facility` (`a facility of kind` `a workplace medical unit`))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2.17, a medical facility` (`a facility of kind` `a private traditional-medicine clinic or diagnosis centre`))
#ASSERT `Article 2.19, a surgery` (`a surgery` (YMD 2026 5 2) (JUST 10) 1000000)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2.19, a surgery` (`A surgery` WITH `date of surgery` IS YMD 2026 5 2, `by licensed surgeons, by hand or with medical equipment, in a hospital` IS TRUE, `in the Ministry of Health list of surgeries` IS FALSE, `percentage in the surgery table` IS JUST 10, `cost of consultation, anaesthesia, the operation and the operating room` IS 1000000))
-- 2.11 is carried as data: 46 items (src:84-92 split on commas).
#ASSERT count `the special diseases listed in Article 2.11` EQUALS 46

§§ `Article 2.18, hospitalisation and its days`

-- Hours recorded: 24 continuous hours is one day; under 24 is no hospitalisation; only whole days
-- count (F12). Hours not recorded: discharge - admission + 1, and two days or more meets the
-- 24-hour test (F11). A 23-hour stay over midnight counts 2 days where hours are not recorded, and
-- a 47-hour stay counts 1 day where they are (finding X8).
#ASSERT `Article 2.18, the days in hospital` (`a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 2) (JUST 24) 0 0) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Article 2.18, a hospitalisation` (`a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 2) (JUST 24) 0 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2.18, a hospitalisation` (`a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 2) (JUST 23) 0 0))
#ASSERT `Article 2.18, the days in hospital` (`a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 3) (JUST 47) 0 0) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Article 2.18, the days in hospital` (`a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 3) (JUST 48) 0 0) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Article 2.18, the days in hospital` (`a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) NOTHING 0 0) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2.18, a hospitalisation` (`a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) NOTHING 0 0))
#ASSERT `Article 2.18, the days in hospital` (`a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 2) NOTHING 0 0) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Article 2.18, a hospitalisation` (`a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 2) NOTHING 0 0)
#ASSERT `Article 2.18, the days in hospital` (`a stay` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 5) NOTHING 0 0) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2.18, a hospitalisation` (`A hospital stay` WITH `admission date` IS YMD 2026 5 1, `discharge date` IS YMD 2026 5 5, `hours in hospital` IS NOTHING, `admission and discharge procedures completed` IS FALSE, `actual reasonable cost of treatment` IS 0, `days already paid this policy year, same kind of medicine` IS 0))

§§ `Article 2.21(b), 2.22(b), when a disability may be certified`

-- Event 1 May 2026. 180 days later is 28 Oct 2026 (May 30 + Jun 30 + Jul 31 + Aug 31 + Sep 30 +
-- Oct 28 = 180); 179 days is 27 Oct.
GIVEN k IS A `A consequence of an accident`
      `certified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`certified in time` k `certified` MEANS
    `Article 2.21(b) or 2.22(b), the certification is not too early` `the accident claim`
        (`an injury` k (YMD 2026 5 1) `certified` (JUST 30) 0 0)

#ASSERT NOT (`certified in time` `total permanent disability by paralysis or assessment` (YMD 2026 10 27))
#ASSERT `certified in time` `total permanent disability by paralysis or assessment` (YMD 2026 10 28)
#ASSERT NOT (`certified in time` `partial permanent disability by loss of function` (YMD 2026 10 27))
#ASSERT `certified in time` `partial permanent disability by loss of function` (YMD 2026 10 28)
#ASSERT `certified in time` `total permanent disability by loss` (YMD 2026 5 2)
#ASSERT `certified in time` `partial permanent disability by loss` (YMD 2026 5 2)

§§ `Article 2.26, dangerous activities`

-- Read literally (F18): climbing counts only "using guidance equipment and/or protective gear",
-- and deep-sea diving only "with a hard helmet and an oxygen tank" (finding X6).
#ASSERT `Article 2.26, a dangerous activity as listed` (`mountain or rock climbing` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2.26, a dangerous activity as listed` (`mountain or rock climbing` FALSE))
#ASSERT `Article 2.26, a dangerous activity as listed` (`deep-sea diving` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 2.26, a dangerous activity as listed` (`deep-sea diving` FALSE))
#ASSERT `Article 2.26, a dangerous activity as listed` `boxing`

§§ `Article 3, double insurance`

#ASSERT `Article 3, the cost left for Tasco` 3000000 1000000 EQUALS 2000000
#ASSERT `Article 3, the cost left for Tasco` 3000000 5000000 EQUALS 0

§§ `Article 4, termination and refunds`

-- In force from the start date to the end date, both included (F20).
#ASSERT `Article 4.1, the contract is in force on` `the illness stay claim` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `Article 4.1, the contract is in force on` `the illness stay claim` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 4.1, the contract is in force on` `the illness stay claim` (YMD 2027 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 4.1, the contract is in force on` `the illness stay claim` (YMD 2025 12 31))

`a state with the premium unpaid on 1 March 2026` MEANS
    `The state of the contract` WITH
        `date the premium was not paid in full or on time`  IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
        `date of an earlier death or total permanent disability of the insured` IS NOTHING
        `date Tasco terminated for ineligibility under Article 4.1(e)` IS NOTHING
        `amount already paid under scope A`                 IS 0
        `amount already paid under scope B`                 IS 0
        `amount already paid under scope C this policy year` IS 0

#ASSERT `Article 4.1, the contract is in force on` (`with the state` `a state with the premium unpaid on 1 March 2026` `the illness stay claim`) (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 4.1, the contract is in force on` (`with the state` `a state with the premium unpaid on 1 March 2026` `the illness stay claim`) (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- 4.1(c) read literally: 20 million paid under scope C (its whole sum insured) ends the whole
-- contract (finding X14); with nothing paid, it does not.
#ASSERT `Article 4.1(c), read literally: the whole contract has ended` (`with the state` (`a state with payments of` 0 `under B and` 20000000 `under C`) `the illness stay claim`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 4.1(c), read literally: the whole contract has ended` `the illness stay claim`)
-- Refunds on a premium of 1,200,000 for a 365-day term with 73 days left: 1,200,000 x 73/365 =
-- 240,000; 4.2(a) pays 70% of that, 168,000, but only if no claim has arisen.
#ASSERT `Article 4.1(e), the refund on termination for ineligibility` 1200000 365 73 EQUALS 240000
#ASSERT `Article 4.2(a), the refund when the policyholder terminates` 1200000 365 73 FALSE EQUALS 168000
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 4.2(a), the refund when the policyholder terminates` 1200000 365 73 TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 4.2(b), the refund when Tasco terminates` 1200000 365 73 EQUALS 240000
-- 4.2 notice at least 30 days before: 1 June to 1 July is 30 days.
#ASSERT `Article 4.2, the notice of termination is in time` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 4.2, the notice of termination is in time` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30))
#ASSERT `Article 4.4, the consequence is within the contract` `the illness stay claim` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 4.4, the consequence is within the contract` `the illness stay claim` (YMD 2027 1 1))

§§ `Article 5, renewal`

GIVEN p IS A `The previous contract`
      k IS A `The contract`
GIVETH A `A claim`
`renewing` p `into` k MEANS
    `with the contract` k (`with the history` (`a renewal of` p `continuous since` (p's `start date`)) `the illness stay claim`)

-- The 2025 contract ended 31 Dec 2025; the 2026 one starts the next day.
#ASSERT `Article 5, the cover is continuous` (`renewing` `the 2025 standard contract` `into` `the standard contract`)
-- Starting on the previous end date is accepted too (F26); a day's gap is not.
#ASSERT `Article 5, the cover is continuous` (`renewing` (`a previous contract` (YMD 2025 1 2) (YMD 2026 1 1) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000)) `into` `the standard contract`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 5, the cover is continuous` (`renewing` (`a previous contract` (YMD 2024 12 31) (YMD 2025 12 30) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000)) `into` `the standard contract`))
-- (4) the previous term a full year: a six-month contract is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 5, the cover is continuous` (`renewing` (`a previous contract` (YMD 2025 7 1) (YMD 2025 12 31) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000)) `into` `the standard contract`))
-- (3) with the second paragraph: an increase keeps continuity for the old part, a decrease or a
-- dropped scope breaks it, an added scope keeps it (F27).
#ASSERT `Article 5, the cover is continuous` (`renewing` (`a previous contract` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 10000000)) `into` `the standard contract`)
#ASSERT `Article 5, the continuous part of the sum insured for` `scope C` `in` (`renewing` (`a previous contract` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 10000000)) `into` `the standard contract`) EQUALS 10000000
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 5, the cover is continuous` (`renewing` (`a previous contract` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 30000000)) `into` `the standard contract`))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 5, the cover is continuous` (`renewing` `the 2025 standard contract` `into` (`a 2026 contract insuring` NOTHING (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000))))
#ASSERT `Article 5, the cover is continuous` (`renewing` (`a previous contract` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) NOTHING) `into` `the standard contract`)
#ASSERT `Article 5, the continuous part of the sum insured for` `scope C` `in` (`renewing` (`a previous contract` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31) (JUST 20000000) (JUST 20000000) NOTHING) `into` `the standard contract`) EQUALS 0
-- (2) the same insured person.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 5, the cover is continuous` (`renewing` (`The previous contract` WITH `start date` IS YMD 2025 1 1, `end date` IS YMD 2025 12 31, `the same insured person` IS FALSE, `sum insured for scope A` IS JUST 20000000, `sum insured for scope B` IS JUST 20000000, `sum insured for scope C` IS JUST 20000000) `into` `the standard contract`))
-- A first contract has nothing to continue.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 5, the cover is continuous` `the illness stay claim`)
#ASSERT `Article 5, Tasco may refuse to renew at the end of the term`

§§ `Article 6`

#ASSERT NOT `Article 6, Tasco accepts a change of benefits during the term`
#ASSERT `Article 6, Tasco may consider a change of benefits at renewal`
